{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02648",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.52,
      "end_seconds": 4.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.41,
      "text": "Right then, come on in. What do you need help with?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 5.54,
      "end_seconds": 12.79,
      "duration_seconds": 7.25,
      "text": "Honestly, um, it's sneezing in spring, and my family pushed me to come."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 14.23,
      "end_seconds": 17.89,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "can you tell me when it first started?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 18.92,
      "end_seconds": 22.96,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "It's been about two weeks, I'm fairly sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 24.65,
      "end_seconds": 27.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "have you tried anything for it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 28.54,
      "end_seconds": 32.72,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "Only antihistamine, uh, and it's not much."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 34.35,
      "end_seconds": 37.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "Right, is it constant or in episodes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 42.54,
      "end_seconds": 45.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "I'd say every other day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 45.64,
      "end_seconds": 48.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "Hm, okay. Does anything set it off?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 49.56,
      "end_seconds": 51.48,
      "duration_seconds": 1.92,
      "text": "It's worse with pollen."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 52.85,
      "end_seconds": 55.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.06,
      "text": "Is it bearing on you a lot?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 57.49,
      "end_seconds": 61.98,
      "duration_seconds": 4.49,
      "text": "I'd give it it a three, out of ten"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 67.82,
      "end_seconds": 70.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "Have you noticed anything else alongside it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 72.53,
      "end_seconds": 81.5,
      "duration_seconds": 8.97,
      "text": "It usually comes with a runny itchy nose. The runny itchy nose? That's been for two months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 82.41,
      "end_seconds": 84.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "Now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.31,
      "end_seconds": 98.1,
      "duration_seconds": 12.79,
      "text": "I'm a bus driver, so I sit for long hours. Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit. No, I share a house with my brother"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 99.14,
      "end_seconds": 103.14,
      "duration_seconds": 4.0,
      "text": "Any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 103.89,
      "end_seconds": 107.92,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "Erm, no, nothing I can think of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.67,
      "end_seconds": 112.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.18,
      "end_seconds": 116.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "No, um, never."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 131.63,
      "end_seconds": 136.21,
      "duration_seconds": 4.58,
      "text": "Can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 137.2,
      "end_seconds": 139.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "Loratadine, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.42,
      "end_seconds": 144.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "Do you know the the dose?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 145.33,
      "end_seconds": 150.12,
      "duration_seconds": 4.79,
      "text": "10 milligrams, I think that's what's on the box."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 150.63,
      "end_seconds": 153.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "Have you got any known allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 154.52,
      "end_seconds": 163.62,
      "duration_seconds": 9.1,
      "text": "Yes, amoxicillin. I've no idea what the reaction was, only that I'm not supposed to have it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.53,
      "end_seconds": 177.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "did you get facial pain or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 179.55,
      "end_seconds": 182.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "No, not a single one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.07,
      "end_seconds": 187.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "Did you get loss of smell or wheeze?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 192.01,
      "end_seconds": 195.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "Mm, no, none of those at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 197.86,
      "end_seconds": 200.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "So, anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 201.34,
      "end_seconds": 204.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "That's normal as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 206.08,
      "end_seconds": 213.95,
      "duration_seconds": 7.87,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. BP is 128 over 70, temperature is 36.8 degrees, pulse is 75 beats a minute."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 215.71,
      "end_seconds": 216.77,
      "duration_seconds": 1.06,
      "text": "Alright, thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.71,
      "end_seconds": 221.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "Shall I start the examination?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 231.83,
      "end_seconds": 234.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "yeah, you know, no problem"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 236.67,
      "end_seconds": 239.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "I'll listen to your chest now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.03,
      "end_seconds": 254.72,
      "duration_seconds": 5.69,
      "text": "The inside of the nose is pale and boggy with clear mucus."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 258.47,
      "end_seconds": 261.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.61,
      "text": "Good, you can sit up again."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 273.66,
      "end_seconds": 286.57,
      "duration_seconds": 12.91,
      "text": "Okay, thinking it through, my working impression is seasonal allergic rhinitis. For this, fluticasone nasal spray, 50 micrograms, once a day, the season. That should help with hay fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 287.45,
      "end_seconds": 289.06,
      "duration_seconds": 1.61,
      "text": "Okay, I understand."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 291.05,
      "end_seconds": 300.03,
      "duration_seconds": 8.98,
      "text": "Shower after being outdoors and keep windows shut when pollen is high. What are the next steps as you understand them?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 301.17,
      "end_seconds": 308.47,
      "duration_seconds": 7.3,
      "text": "so, I take the fluticasone nasal spray, 50 micrograms, once a day is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 309.9,
      "end_seconds": 314.91,
      "duration_seconds": 5.01,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Alright, I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 315.82,
      "end_seconds": 319.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "Good, thanks, I'll see you then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 320.72,
      "end_seconds": 321.9,
      "duration_seconds": 1.18,
      "text": "Look after yourself."
    }
  ]
}